#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
tv - Twitch/YouTube companion for the Omarchy "TV" shell plugin.

The QML bar widget shells out to this script; everything that touches the
network, OAuth, or the media player lives here so it can be tested on its own.

Commands:
  tv setup                         Print the setup walkthrough
  tv creds set [--twitch-client-id ...] [--youtube-client-id ...]
                                   [--youtube-client-secret ...]
  tv creds show
  tv auth twitch                   Device-code login (bundled Client ID; no setup)
  tv auth youtube                  Device-code login (needs youtube client id+secret)
  tv auth logout <twitch|youtube|all>
  tv status [--json]               Auth + player + counts
  tv live [--json] [--platform twitch|youtube] [--no-cache]
                                   Channels live right now that you follow
  tv search <query> [--json] [--platform ...] [--live-only]
  tv fav <list|add|remove|toggle> [platform] [id] [--json]
  tv watch <url|twitch-login>      Open in mpv (falls back to browser)
  tv chat <url|twitch-login>       Toggle a chat window docked next to mpv
                                   [--toggle] [--close] [--width N]
  tv open <url>                    Open in the default browser

All state lives under ~/.local/state/omarchy/tv/, credentials under
~/.config/omarchy/tv/credentials.json.
"""

